// NOT PART OF THE PUBLIC API. See wayland_platform.cpp for the documented
// Wayland limitations (no global position, compositor owned decorations, focus
// dependent clipboard) and the threading model.
//
// The xdg-shell protocol code is generated by wayland-scanner at build time
// (see CMakeLists.txt). CMake only enables this backend when wayland-scanner and
// wayland-protocols are present - in AUTO mode it falls back to X11 instead - so
// NATIVEBRIDGE_HAVE_XDG_SHELL is always defined for a Wayland build. The
// remaining #ifdef guards only keep the header self contained for tooling that
// compiles the file without the generated header.

